Bugfix: Raise the text contrasts left on the brand turquoise

Eight places in the interface carried text below the 4.5:1 minimum: the active
and disabled state of primary buttons, the selected day of the date picker, the
alternative login buttons, system tag chips, the sub-tab headers of the share
dialog, the database picker of the installer and the success message of the
settings pages. The worst of them reached 1.17:1.

Seven shared one cause. The design integration replaced the previous dark fill
with the brand turquoise without adjusting the light text colours that sat on
it. Those places now use dark text on the unchanged brand colour, which reaches
7.31:1 and leaves the brand tone itself alone. The sub-tab header and the
success message needed their own values and received them.

The disabled state of primary buttons no longer keeps a muted grey on the full
brand fill. Text in inactive components is exempt from the contrast
requirement, but a dead control that looks like the most prominent live one is
misleading, so it now uses the muted surface the login page already applies.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 1.4.3
